    <string-array name="welcome_points">
        <item>Register the specimen: home planet and subspecies. The bureau knows their traits and weak spots.</item>
        <item>Keep the log in two taps: mood, appetite, weight. Photograph the specimen and tag what it does – poses open up the behaviour atlas.</item>
        <item>New food, medicine or a move is an experiment: write a hypothesis, then the result.</item>
        <item>Every Sunday a typed report arrives, with your photos and conclusions.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_station">
        <item>The station</item>
        <item>A folder per specimen. The four buttons under the card log the most common things in a tap.</item>
        <item>Life support due soon is below: tick it when done.</item>
        <item>Integrity drops when protocols are overdue. Nothing terrible happens – the bureau just frowns.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_atlas">
        <item>The behaviour atlas</item>
        <item>Every pose and habit of the planet has a number.</item>
        <item>An entry opens when you tag your own photo with it: the photo becomes its picture.</item>
        <item>Rare entries have three dots. Some take months to catch.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_reports">
        <item>Reports</item>
        <item>A week of observation becomes a typed report on Sunday evening.</item>
        <item>Photos go in with captions, new skills get a stamp.</item>
        <item>Share a report as a picture. Designs are bought with grants.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_course">
        <item>The course</item>
        <item>Short lessons about your specimen’s planet: body language, stress, food, health.</item>
        <item>Each has a field task to do with your own animal and one question.</item>
        <item>Grants raise your rank from laboratory assistant to academician.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_dossier">
        <item>The file</item>
        <item>The radar shows the traits: dashed is the subspecies norm, solid is what you observed.</item>
        <item>Predispositions are what this breed tends to suffer from: worth knowing early.</item>
        <item>At the bottom is the extract for the vet: a PDF with everything they’ll ask.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_trial">
        <item>An experiment</item>
        <item>Anything new is an experiment: food, medicine, a move, guests.</item>
        <item>Write what you expect – then conclude whether the hypothesis held.</item>
        <item>The ethics committee reads every application. It won’t let anyone frighten or poison the specimen.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_shot">
        <item>A field photo</item>
        <item>After this memo the camera opens.</item>
        <item>Then tag what the photo shows: belly up, loaf, ambush.</item>
        <item>The first tag is the main one: it becomes the caption in the weekly report.</item>
    </string-array>
